WHY GPL v3, AND WHY IT IS NOT A PREFERENCE
------------------------------------------

Loom draws its window with PyQt6, which is licensed GPL-3.0-only. A
distributed binary that bundles PyQt6 is a combined work, and GPL v3 is
what that combination requires. This is not a position taken on software
freedom - it is the licence the dependency already imposes, and choosing a
permissive licence for Loom while shipping PyQt6 inside the .exe would be a
violation rather than a choice.

Two things GPL v3 does NOT prevent, since both are commonly assumed:
donations are entirely unaffected, and selling copies is expressly
permitted. What it requires is that whoever receives the program can also
receive its source and the same rights.

The only route to a permissive licence would be replacing PyQt6 with
PySide6, which is LGPL. That is a real migration across every Qt file plus
a re-verification of the overlay's X11 passthrough, and it has not been
done. Anyone tempted to "simplify" this to MIT should start there.


THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
----------------------

Bundled in the distributed application:

  PyQt6                    GPL-3.0-only          <- the binding constraint
  PyQt6-Qt6                LGPL v3
  NumPy                    BSD-3-Clause (and 0BSD, MIT, Zlib, CC0-1.0)
  OpenCV (headless)        Apache License 2.0
  mss                      MIT

Per platform:

  windows-capture          MIT                   Windows only
  pywin32                  PSF                   Windows only
  python-xlib              LGPL v2.1 or later    Linux only
  pyobjc                   MIT                   macOS only

Development only, not distributed:

  mgz                      MIT                   reads recorded games
  construct                MIT                   a dependency of mgz
  pytest, PyInstaller, Pillow

A note for anyone auditing this: Apache License 2.0 is compatible with GPL
version 3 but NOT with version 2, which is one of the reasons this project
is on v3 specifically and must not be moved back.


AGE OF EMPIRES II
-----------------

Loom is an unofficial third-party tool. It is not affiliated with,
endorsed by, or connected to Microsoft, Xbox Game Studios, Forgotten
Empires or World's Edge. Age of Empires is a trademark of Microsoft
Corporation.

Loom reads the game's screen and never touches the game process. The one
thing it takes FROM the game is a registered keyboard shortcut, which is
why every binding is editable and every one can be emptied.
